= Context (linguistics) — Simple =

'''Context''' is the information around language that helps people understand what it means.

If someone says “I am here now,” you need to know who is speaking, where they are, and when they said it.

Context can include:

* words and sentences that came before;
* the speaker and listener;
* time and place;
* things people can see;
* what people already know or assume;
* the situation and goal of the conversation.

[[Common ground/Simple|Common ground]] is part of context, but it is not all of context.

Context is especially important in [[Pragmatics/Simple|pragmatics]], where people study how language is understood in real situations.

